&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a skilled and detail-oriented U.S. International Tax Manager to join our global tax team. In this role, you will oversee the company’s U.S. international tax planning, compliance, and reporting, ensuring alignment with business objectives while navigating complex tax laws. Working closely with internal and external stakeholders, you will drive the delivery of effective tax strategies and maintain compliance within an ever-evolving international tax landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role can be based out of our Austin office or remotely in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance and Reporting: Manage and oversee U.S. international tax compliance, including forms such as Form 5471, Form 8858, Form 8865, and foreign tax credit calculations, ensuring accurate and timely filings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tax Planning: Provide technical expertise in the analysis, implementation, and optimization of U.S. international tax strategies, including GILTI, Subpart F, FDII, BEAT, and foreign tax credits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global Tax Operations: Support the preparation and review of quarterly and annual tax provisions, specifically focusing on international tax components of ASC 740 reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tax Research: Conduct detailed research on U.S. international tax laws, treaty benefits, and implications of legislative changes (e.g., OECD BEPS, U.S. Tax Reform), and provide actionable guidance to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: Partner with finance, legal, accounting, and other teams to advise on tax-efficient strategies for cross-border transactions, acquisitions, and expansions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tax Technology: Support process improvement initiatives related to tax automation, efficiency, and the use of tax software tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit Support: Assist with tax audits and reviews conducted by U.S. or foreign tax authorities, including preparing documentation and managing information requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s Degree in Accounting, Finance, Taxation, or a related field. CPA, JD, or advanced degree in Taxation (e.g., MST) strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7 years of relevant experience in U.S. international tax within public accounting, a corporate tax department, or consulting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical knowledge of U.S. international tax laws, including GILTI, Subpart F, FDII, BEAT, foreign tax credits, and treaty applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in ASC 740 (accounting for income taxes), particularly for international tax provisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience with U.S. compliance software such as Corptax, OneSource, or similar tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent research and analytical skills with the ability to synthesize complex concepts and communicate recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously in a deadline-driven environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
