&lt;li&gt;Set the vision and strategy for candidate experience globally, ensuring a consistent, high-quality, and equitable experience across all regions and hiring stages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve the candidate journey from interview scheduling through offer acceptance, identifying friction points and implementing scalable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain reporting dashboards to track key metrics such as scheduling SLAs, candidate satisfaction (NPS), and coordinator productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently monitor and forecast team capacity, ensuring regional teams are appropriately staffed to meet hiring volume&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally to align candidate experience initiatives with broader talent strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption of new tools and automation to increase coordinator efficiency using AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in recruiting coordination, recruiting operations, or talent acquisition, with at least 3 years in a people management role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing distributed or global teams across multiple time zones and regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the candidate lifecycle and best practices for high-volume, high-quality interview experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational mindset with a track record of building scalable processes and driving measurable improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ATS platforms (Greenhouse preferred) and scheduling tools; comfort with data and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
