&lt;p&gt;REQ ID: 4263305802&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;MongoDB’s base salary range for this role is posted below. Compensation at the time of offer is unique to each candidate and based on a variety of factors such as skill set, experience, qualifications, and work location. Salary is one part of MongoDB’s total compensation and benefits package. Other benefits for eligible employees may include: equity, participation in the employee stock purchase program, flexible paid time off, 20 weeks fully-paid gender-neutral parental leave, fertility and adoption assistance, 401(k) plan, mental health counseling, access to transgender-inclusive health insurance coverage, and health benefits offerings. Please note, the base salary range listed below and the benefits in this paragraph are only applicable to U.S.-based candidates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;MongoDB’s base salary range for this role in the U.S. is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$136,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$266,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Build &amp;amp; Grow Developer Relations Team enables our most strategic customers to effectively use MongoDB technology. This team is the tip of the spear within these accounts, working with their developers as well as key internal MongoDB stakeholders (e.g., Sales, Marketing), to encourage adoption of MongoDB solutions. We&#39;re seeking a Senior Developer Advocate to join our team and drive developer enablement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to capture the imagination of new and potential MongoDB developers within these accounts, to enable developers as they begin their MongoDB journey, and to lead developers in designs for new or replatformed workloads. Our team increases developers’ effective use of MongoDB and reduces the time it takes for developers to meaningfully use the platform. You will join a team of our most experienced engineers and host virtual and in-person engagement with customers throughout the world. If you’re passionate about data and helping developers create some of the most performant, scalable, and efficient solutions of their careers, then join us in shaping the future of development on MongoDB.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our Developer Relations teams are distributed around the world and a majority of the group works remotely. This is a UK / Europe based role primarily working with customers in the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role can be based remotely in the Ireland region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Candidate Profile&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Developer Advocate, you are a competent developer ready to peer, mentor, and lead development teams as they solve their enterprise&#39;s most critical data issues. You are familiar with MongoDB or other data technologies and otherwise have the ability to quickly become proficient in MongoDB, possess insight into developer enablement programs and have the ability to guide development teams in the adoption of new technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re an excellent public speaker and are comfortable delivering live enablement sessions to technical audiences of up to 400 or more. Your recent experience includes directly enabling developers and architects with data-related challenges and moving them toward solutions for their real-world performance and scalability problems. As a bonus, your experience also includes exercising soft leadership with decision makers in organizations for defining, adopting, and scaling data-related technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a combination of software engineering, solutions development, consulting experience, and developer relations, you have a deep understanding of developer ecosystems and how developers best acquire fluency in new technologies. You have a solid working knowledge of databases, database performance, schema design, and optimizing production applications at scale. You employ a well-developed consulting method that allows you to quickly triage situations to understand the most critical issues at hand and to address them efficiently.&amp;nbsp; Finally, you excel at explaining complex technical concepts in simple terms and have a natural ability to connect and communicate with developers of various skill levels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaboration and empowerment are at the heart of this team’s work style. You&#39;ll work closely with other team members to create and refine content, to deliver events, and to share insights, techniques, and best practices with the larger MongoDB team and with the broader developer community. Your focus is not just on individual success but on success of the entire team, consistent with MongoDB&#39;s value of Building Together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Position Expectations&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become a Subject Matter Expert on document schema design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop an understanding of core MongoDB database functionality and Atlas features such as Search, Vector Search, Data Federation, Online Archive, and Streaming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver Design Review sessions to customer development teams in order to guide their design and use of MongoDB document schemas for their specific workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate insights gathered from developer engagement, through code and content, to inform team members and enable other developers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver virtual and in-person developer enablement sessions to audiences of up to 400 developers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create language-specific or other content in your area of expertise to evangelize and educate various developer communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of experience in both customer-facing and developer-centric roles such as Consulting, Solutions Architecture, Developer Relations, working with development teams in the design of document schemas and high performance, scalable database implementations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3 years of experience (or the equivalent) of consulting with development teams as a non-member of the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with at least one of the languages most popular with our customers (Java, Python, Javascript)&lt;br&gt;Familiarity with 2 or more of the languages popular with our customers (Java, Python, Javascript or Typescript, C#, Rust, PHP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in creating effective developer-focused code and content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills, with ability in conducting live streams, or public speaking at events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Written and spoken English language proficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and willingness to travel (up to 50%) primarily within the UK, Europe, with some travel to India / Asia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
