&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is seeking a highly motivated Senior Manager, Strategic Finance. You will be responsible for driving key strategic financial initiatives and providing financial insights to support decision-making and drive the company’s growth. In this role, you will sit at the intersection of FP&amp;amp;A, sales, product, marketing and investor relations and work closely with the executive team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a hybrid in-office role. We are looking for candidates who plan to be available in our New York City office for approximately 2-3 days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a high-performing finance team responsible for the company&#39;s revenue model inclusive of the quarterly, annual, and long term revenue forecasting based on a variety of bottoms up and top down methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strategic advisor to GTM leadership, including Sales and Marketing teams, providing data-driven insights and financial guidance to drive revenue growth and achieve financial objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and set targets for our GTM, Marketing, and select Product teams based on historical productivity and expected performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the company’s gross profit forecast, including forecasting infrastructure and services margins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the company’s direct cash flow forecast, working closely with accounting and treasury / tax teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and maintain detailed long-range plans, providing insights that support strategic decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the entire FP&amp;amp;A team on creating and maintaining the consolidated company financial model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain scalable processes to enhance visibility into financial forecasts and performance, collaborating with teams across the business to maximize predictability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive special projects and conduct ad-hoc analyses to support decision making, including M&amp;amp;A, new products, markets, and other growth initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support investor relations efforts through financial analysis for guidance, Q&amp;amp;A prep and creating materials for the annual investor day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare presentations and analysis for executive leadership, Board of Directors and investors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Requirements:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant finance experience, with a strong preference for candidates with an investment banking background and subsequent experience in strategic finance, corporate development, or principal investing roles. Experience in enterprise tech or with consumption business models is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in financial modeling, with the ability to develop and manage complex models and frameworks that can be leveraged to drive decision-making&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical capabilities and business acumen with ability to apply rigorous logic to solve multi-facested problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in building strong working relationships with cross-functional business partners and leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence with proven ability to influence and effectively synthesize key findings and trends into actionable insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
