&lt;p&gt;The IT Go-to-Market organization builds and operates the technology platforms that power Sales, Marketing, and Revenue Operations. These products enable scalable lead generation, pipeline management, deal execution, and revenue insights across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Manager on the IT Go-to-Market (GTM) team, you will own internal technology products that support critical GTM capabilities such as CRM platforms, lead-to-quote workflows, sales productivity tools, and marketing automation systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Sales, Marketing and RevOps&amp;nbsp; teams to define product strategy, prioritize initiatives, and deliver solutions that improve seller productivity, accelerate deal execution, and enable data-driven decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Strategy &amp;amp; Vision&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and communicate the product vision and roadmap for GTM technology platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business strategy and operational needs into scalable product capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve seller productivity, marketing effectiveness, and revenue workflows through technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align product strategy with enterprise architecture, security, and platform standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Lifecycle Ownership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end lifecycle of GTM products from discovery and requirements through delivery and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop clear product requirements (PRDs), define success metrics, and track product adoption and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use user feedback and data insights to refine priorities and improve the product experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stakeholder Engagement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Marketing, RevOps, Finance, Security, and IT teams to understand pain points and identify opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the voice of the user, ensuring solutions address real operational challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate priorities, trade-offs, timelines, and progress clearly to stakeholders and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong partnerships with engineering teams, architects, and external vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roadmap &amp;amp; Delivery&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and maintain the product backlog and roadmap, prioritizing work based on business impact and technical feasibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with engineering teams in an Agile environment to plan and deliver product releases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance new feature development with platform improvements and technical debt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure smooth product delivery by managing cross-team dependencies and aligning stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Adoption &amp;amp; Change Management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with enablement and change management teams to drive adoption of new GTM capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate product changes and new features across impacted teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor KPIs and support incident or problem management when issues arise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in product management, ideally supporting enterprise or internal technology platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Go-to-Market systems such as CRM platforms, marketing automation tools, or lead-to-quote workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to translate business needs into clear product strategy, requirements, and roadmap priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with engineering teams in Agile delivery environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills across business and technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency in enterprise systems, integrations, and SaaS platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills with the ability to explain complex technical and business concepts to diverse audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Salesforce or comparable CRM platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with&amp;nbsp;AI-enabled GTM workflows or automation tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using&amp;nbsp;product metrics and analytics to guide decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related field (or equivalent experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
